A rendering engine converts HTML, CSS and other web resources into the visual webpage displayed by the browser.

Browser	Rendering Engine
Google Chrome	Blink
Microsoft Edge	Blink
Mozilla Firefox	Gecko
Safari	WebKit
Opera	Blink
Difference

Blink

Used by Chrome, Edge, Opera and many Chromium-based browsers.
Developed as part of the Chromium project.

Gecko

Used by Firefox.
Developed by Mozilla.

WebKit

Used by Safari.
Developed by Apple and the WebKit community.

Different rendering engines may interpret some newer or unusual web features differently, so developers test websites across multiple browsers.